  "title": "Greg W NDE",
  "date": "2025-05-03T00:08:08.000Z",
  "content": "I was driven to the hospital, after my neurologist discovered that one side of my heart was not functioning correctly. <br><br>I barely made it to the car. My wife was driving us to the hospital, as the doctor did not think we had enough time to call a paramedic. <br><br>While lying in the car, I found myself standing in the most complete darkness I have ever experienced. As I looked down, I could see my body. I was standing at the edge of what I perceived to be a cliff of some kind. I felt like there was a deep void in front of me. I had a decision to make. I told myself, 'Not now,' as it was not my time to go yet. <br><br> I woke up in the emergency room with a pacemaker attached to my leg. That's my experience. There was no floating, light, loving feelings, or God. There was just darkness. I was then life-flighted to Denver, where I spent 2 weeks in the hospital. <br><br><span class=\"m108",
